<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>orrery daily use</title>
<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { margin: 0 auto; max-width: 56rem; padding: 2rem 1rem; font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; background: #ffffff; color: #1f2328; }
h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.6rem 0 0.4rem; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 0.2rem 1rem 0.2rem 0; }
th { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background: #0d1117; color: #e6edf3; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>orrery daily use</h1>
<h2>p</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>p</th><td>attach the most recently active session, then open the tree</td></tr>
<tr><th>p .</th><td>the session for the current directory, created if missing</td></tr>
<tr><th>p WORD</th><td>a session named WORD, else a zoxide match, else the picker</td></tr>
<tr><th>p new NAME</th><td>create project directory NAME and a session for it (--root DIR sets the parent)</td></tr>
<tr><th>p WORDS...</th><td>open the picker with WORDS as the intent</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>tmux (prefix is C-a)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>prefix Space</th><td>open the tree in a popup</td></tr>
<tr><th>prefix s</th><td>open the shell popup for the current pane&#39;s directory</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>kitty</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>kitty_mod&#43;p</th><td>run p; nix-config&#39;s kitty binding, not set by orrery</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>tree</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>j, down</th><td>move the cursor one row down</td></tr>
<tr><th>k, up</th><td>move the cursor one row up</td></tr>
<tr><th>n</th><td>move to the next unseen row after the cursor, wrapping around</td></tr>
<tr><th>/</th><td>start filter input. Typed text sets the filter. Backspace deletes its last character, Enter keeps the filter, and Esc clears it</td></tr>
<tr><th>enter</th><td>switch the client to the row&#39;s pane, mark the pane seen, and close the tree</td></tr>
<tr><th>x</th><td>mark the row&#39;s pane seen; the tree stays open</td></tr>
<tr><th>c</th><td>add a window running `claude` to the row&#39;s session, started in the row&#39;s directory; the tree stays open</td></tr>
<tr><th>s</th><td>open the shell popup for the row&#39;s directory, and close the tree</td></tr>
<tr><th>N</th><td>close the tree and run the picker for the row&#39;s directory; the picker&#39;s choice switches the client</td></tr>
<tr><th>X</th><td>close the row&#39;s pane after a y/N prompt, asking twice for a working Claude pane</td></tr>
<tr><th>D</th><td>close every session of the row&#39;s project and its shell session after a prompt listing them</td></tr>
<tr><th>?</th><td>show every key</td></tr>
<tr><th>esc, q</th><td>close the tree</td></tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
